WEBVTT

00:09.493 --> 00:11.675
Welcome back to the Engine Room Records

00:11.755 --> 00:12.596
Planetarium.

00:14.998 --> 00:19.082
Following the fragmentation event, the

00:19.163 --> 00:21.185
central engine has been salvaged and

00:21.245 --> 00:24.288
transported to the Star City Orbital Ward.

00:26.810 --> 00:29.773
Diagnostics indicate a complete and permanent

00:29.933 --> 00:32.636
severing of the T-10 power conduit.

00:35.437 --> 00:38.282
Automated systems below the damage threshold

00:38.342 --> 00:42.849
have officially failed. Strict manual

00:42.909 --> 00:47.576
maintenance protocols must now be initiated to

00:47.636 --> 00:49.419
ensure system survival.

01:15.771 --> 01:21.698
Strap down to the diagnostic bed Static and the

01:21.858 --> 01:26.543
sirens ringing in my head They towed the broken

01:26.683 --> 01:32.009
metal to the star city dock Now I'm running my

01:32.029 --> 01:37.694
life on a four hour clock The automated systems

01:37.875 --> 01:42.097
are completely dead I've got to run the heavy

01:42.277 --> 01:48.301
engine on the manual instead The T-10 conduit is

01:48.421 --> 01:52.803
severed in the dark I lost the lower thrusters

01:52.903 --> 01:57.586
but I still have the spark Lock the iron dome,

01:57.626 --> 02:02.772
keep the perimeter tight I'm learning how to fly

02:02.852 --> 02:08.262
it in the middle of the night. Star City Orbital

02:08.322 --> 02:14.524
Ward. Strapped to the table, strapped to the

02:14.644 --> 02:18.025
board I hate the heavy chair, I hate the

02:18.146 --> 02:22.407
diagnostic room But I'm pushing through the

02:22.547 --> 02:26.208
fire and I'm pushing through the gloom I've got a

02:26.288 --> 02:30.510
crew to lift me, I've got a spotter on the time A

02:31.390 --> 02:35.511
heavy metal mountain that I still have to climb

02:35.551 --> 02:36.892
In the orbital ward

02:41.240 --> 02:45.325
Every 15 minutes I've got to shift the weight

02:46.186 --> 02:50.091
Trying to keep the pressure off, trying to stay

02:50.211 --> 02:53.955
straight The freight dogs pull me up the

02:54.116 --> 02:59.682
maintenance hatch A synchronized lift, a heavy

02:59.782 --> 03:04.446
metal catch My hands are on the console, I've got

03:04.506 --> 03:09.068
the upper gear We're rewriting the protocols

03:09.188 --> 03:15.331
right out here The T-10 conduit is severed in the

03:15.391 --> 03:19.913
dark I lost the lower thrusters, but I still have

03:19.973 --> 03:23.915
the spark Lock the iron, don't keep the

03:24.035 --> 03:29.383
perimeter tight I'm learning how to fly it in the

03:29.423 --> 03:34.694
middle of the night! Star City Orbital Ward!

03:36.522 --> 03:41.384
Strapped to the table, strapped to the board I

03:41.424 --> 03:45.925
hate the heavy chair, I hate the diagnostic room

03:46.425 --> 03:50.106
But I'm pushing through the fire and I'm pushing

03:50.166 --> 03:53.927
through the gloom I've got a crew to lift me, I've

03:53.987 --> 03:58.889
got a spotter on the time A heavy metal mountain

03:58.909 --> 04:02.650
that I still have to climb in the orbital ward

04:29.097 --> 04:30.479
The connection is broken.

04:33.341 --> 04:34.962
But the hands still work.

04:38.548 --> 04:39.869
The legs are silent.

04:43.091 --> 04:49.456
But the engine still roars! Star City Orbital

04:49.516 --> 04:55.877
Ward! Strapped to the table, strapped to the

04:55.997 --> 04:59.399
board I hate the heavy chair, I hate the

04:59.479 --> 05:03.720
diagnostic room But I'm pushing through the

05:03.860 --> 05:07.541
fire and I'm pushing through the gloom I've got a

05:07.621 --> 05:11.763
